Keep the suite enabled on slow RISC-V builders: allow cold imports and bounded
CPU work to finish, wait for asynchronous cleanup, avoid unsupported mobilecli
binary probes, and leave terminal mock SSE streams open until abort so
one-millisecond replay loops cannot starve React act.

Cleanup-retry precedent:
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/pull/8982
Bounded sanitizer input retained; assignment matching scans separators and their
adjacent identifiers. Start JWT matching only at a base64url token boundary,
not at every hyphen, to avoid quadratic rescans under the original deadline:
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/pull/7877
Worker-log redaction keeps a 20-second complexity bound, as upstream does for
contended builders, rather than disabling its timing assertion:
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/pull/10912
Shell-safety complexity-budget precedent:
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/pull/10735
Mobilecli maps every non-arm64 architecture to its amd64 binary:
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/blob/v0.21.10/packages/mobile-mcp/src/mobilecli.ts#L99-L103

Mem0 duplicates the JWT scan and uses local HTTP deadlines too short for RISC-V.
Retain the sanitizer bound, cumulative deadline, and no-retry assertions:
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/pull/11246
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/pull/11311
https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/pull/11337

